Z||000005||Ken Wittlief||11-24-2001||08:33 AM||||the ribbed screen is a big fresnel lens - the projector doenst need one to work - in fact you could take the guts out of the projector and point it at a white wall in a pinch except, unless the projector has a front/rear switch the image will be mirrored.<P> you can also project it on the backside of a sheet, and it will show through.<P> I have an LCD based projector - I was an engineer at Sayett Technology, the company that invented LCD projection, and I have a couple of engineering protoype units that they were going to throw out.<P> One is mounted on the ceiling in my basement pointed at a white sheet that is hung on a ten foot piece of conduit at the other end of the room.<P> the only problem with using a wall instead of the fresnel is the image will not be as bright.<P> I gather from your first post you want to fix the unit like it was, but if not, you do have other options.<P> Im pretty sure you can buy the fresnel at photo/video shops - some people put them in the wall, and have the projector in a small room behind the wall - so they are available for that purpose - maybe you can get one the right size to match.||||reg||1
